<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:29:30 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>哀悼者将一个古老的吸管杯放在罗马幼儿的坟墓中。它可能是为了维持孩子的来世之旅</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mourners-laced-an-ancient-sippy-cup-in-a-roman-toddlers-grave-it-may-have-been-meant-to-sustain-the-child-on-the-journey-to-the-afterlife-180989673/</link><description>十多年前在英国出土了被称为“tettina”的喷嘴杯碎片。最近已修复并首次展出</description><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:44:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mourners-laced-an-ancient-sippy-cup-in-a-roman-toddlers-grave-it-may-have-been-meant-to-sustain-the-child-on-the-journey-to-the-afterlife-180989673/</guid></item><item><title>一群谷仓猫头鹰搬进了纽约市上西区，这可能是现代历史上第一个在曼哈顿筑巢的猫头鹰家族</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-family-of-barn-owls-has-moved-into-new-york-citys-upper-west-side-perhaps-the-first-to-nest-in-manhattan-in-modern-history-180989674/</link><description>这些长着羽毛的居民引起了广泛的关注，因为它们的物种被认为是城市中极为罕见的景观</description><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:25:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-family-of-barn-owls-has-moved-into-new-york-citys-upper-west-side-perhaps-the-first-to-nest-in-manhattan-in-modern-history-180989674/</guid></item><item><title>世界上最大的帽带企鹅群之一正在迅速缩小</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/one-of-the-worlds-largest-chinstrap-penguin-colonies-is-shrinking-fast-180989676/</link><description>扎沃多夫斯基岛是南美洲和南极洲之间的一个偏远无人居住的火山岛，根据一项新研究，2011 年至 2025 年间，该岛的帽带企鹅减少了 63%</description><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:23:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/one-of-the-worlds-largest-chinstrap-penguin-colonies-is-shrinking-fast-180989676/</guid></item><item><title>第二次世界大战期间，一架美国轰炸机坠入英国荒原，一名下士被宣布在行动中失踪。考古学家现在重新开始寻找他的遗骸</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/after-an-american-bomber-crashed-into-an-english-moor-during-world-war-II-a-corporal-was-declared-missing-in-action-archaeologists-have-now-revived-the-search-for-his-remains-180989672/</link><description>克拉伦斯·沃森 (Clarence Watson) 下士是一架 B-24H 解放者号在大雾条件下坠毁的 10 名美国飞行员之一。机组人员正在为“Carpetbagger 行动”进行训练，这是一项绝密行动，旨在深入纳粹占领的欧洲</description><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:58:31 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/after-an-american-bomber-crashed-into-an-english-moor-during-world-war-II-a-corporal-was-declared-missing-in-action-archaeologists-have-now-revived-the-search-for-his-remains-180989672/</guid></item><item><title>在西班牙的一个岩石庇护所中发现的史无前例的古代木制工具宝藏表明尼安德特人是熟练的木工</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-unprecedented-trove-of-ancient-wooden-tools-uncovered-at-a-rock-shelter-in-spain-show-neanderthals-were-skilled-woodworkers-180989668/</link><description>木制物品通常会很快分解，但周期性的洪水和水中的矿物质有助于在一个名为 Abric Romaní 的地点保存这些物品。考古学家记录了近 600 件木制品或其印记，其中 13 件明显是由人手塑造的</description><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:00:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-unprecedented-trove-of-ancient-wooden-tools-uncovered-at-a-rock-shelter-in-spain-show-neanderthals-were-skilled-woodworkers-180989668/</guid></item><item><title>在家族财富和 Instagram 的帮助下，Z 世代在艺术市场上大手笔花钱</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/with-the-help-of-family-wealth-and-instagram-gen-z-is-spending-big-in-the-art-market-180989664/</link><description>一项新调查显示，20 多岁的高净值人群正在成为全球艺术品交易中最活跃的成员，其支出大幅超过其他几代人。他们的习惯正在改变艺术世界的运作方式</description><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:19:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/with-the-help-of-family-wealth-and-instagram-gen-z-is-spending-big-in-the-art-market-180989664/</guid></item><item><title>这个撒丁岛小村庄可能是一个新的“蓝色区域”，并且可能蕴藏着女性长寿的秘密</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-tiny-sardinian-village-might-be-a-new-blue-zone-and-could-hold-the-secrets-to-female-longevity-180989660/</link><description>一项新研究显示，在意大利岛上的博洛塔纳小镇，约有 2,300 名居民，70 岁以上的女性活到 100 岁的可能性大约是美国女性的三倍</description><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-tiny-sardinian-village-might-be-a-new-blue-zone-and-could-hold-the-secrets-to-female-longevity-180989660/</guid></item><item><title>志愿者正在帮助发掘英格兰最古老的麻风病医院之一，让人们一睹中世纪时期麻风病受害者的待遇</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/volunteers-are-helping-unearth-one-of-englands-oldest-leprosy-hospitals-giving-a-glimpse-into-how-victims-of-the-disease-were-treated-in-medieval-times-180989665/</link><description>研究人员认为，建于 11 世纪或 12 世纪的圣婴医院可能拥有“带小院子的小房子”，可容纳多达 20 名麻风病患者。 “你需要有资源才能进入这里，”一位考古学家说。</description><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:13:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/volunteers-are-helping-unearth-one-of-englands-oldest-leprosy-hospitals-giving-a-glimpse-into-how-victims-of-the-disease-were-treated-in-medieval-times-180989665/</guid></item><item><title>工业化摧毁了我们的微生物组吗？对南美洲和非洲农村觅食社区的一项新研究表明答案是肯定的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/did-industrialization-gut-our-microbiomes-a-new-study-on-rural-foraging-communities-in-south-america-and-africa-hints-the-answer-is-yes-180989658/</link><description>两个群体——玻利维亚的提斯曼采集园艺者和坦桑尼亚的哈扎狩猎采集者——拥有超过 1,200 种肠道微生物。然而，据研究人员称，其中约 60% 的特征在生活在工业化地区的人们中很少见或不存在</description><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/did-industrialization-gut-our-microbiomes-a-new-study-on-rural-foraging-communities-in-south-america-and-africa-hints-the-answer-is-yes-180989658/</guid></item><item><title>在史密森保护生物学研究所的直播中观看五只可爱的新生猎豹幼崽的成长</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/watch-five-adorable-newborn-cheetah-cubs-grow-on-a-livestream-from-the-smithsonians-conservation-biology-institute-180989669/</link><description>这些健康活泼的小宝宝正在由初为人母的祖拉 (Zura) 照顾，公众可以通过在线猎豹幼崽摄像头了解它们的滑稽动作</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 21:05:40 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/watch-five-adorable-newborn-cheetah-cubs-grow-on-a-livestream-from-the-smithsonians-conservation-biology-institute-180989669/</guid></item><item><title>借助尖端技术，纽约现代艺术博物馆将打造一座数字沼泽，将您包裹在大自然中</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-digital-swamp-coming-to-new-york-citys-moma-is-made-to-envelop-you-in-nature-with-the-help-of-cutting-edge-technology-180989652/</link><description>“湿地”是丹麦艺术家雅各布·库斯克·斯廷森设计的高科技巡回展览的最新装置。它借助民间传说、音景和视频游戏软件，重建了被忽视的生态系统</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 20:39:30 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-digital-swamp-coming-to-new-york-citys-moma-is-made-to-envelop-you-in-nature-with-the-help-of-cutting-edge-technology-180989652/</guid></item><item><title>2026 年诺贝尔和平奖获得者纳维·皮莱在种族隔离的南非长大，是世界领先的人权法学家之一</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/raised-in-apartheid-south-africa-2026-nobel-peace-prize-winner-navi-pillay-is-one-of-the-worlds-leading-human-rights-jurists-180989667/</link><description>当皮莱得知自己获奖时，她正身处纽伦堡审判追究纳粹战犯责任的同一法庭。她的法律职业生涯致力于打击侵犯人权和大规模暴行</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 18:53:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/raised-in-apartheid-south-africa-2026-nobel-peace-prize-winner-navi-pillay-is-one-of-the-worlds-leading-human-rights-jurists-180989667/</guid></item><item><title>科学家从世界上最古老的乌龟身上取出了脸颊拭子。他的DNA可能揭示长寿的线索</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-took-a-cheek-swab-from-the-worlds-oldest-tortoise-his-dna-could-reveal-hints-to-longevity-180989663/</link><description>乔纳森是一只亚达伯拉象龟，大约 194 岁，是当今现存最古老的陆地动物。关于他的遗传学的发现可以为延长人类寿命提供线索</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 17:28:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-took-a-cheek-swab-from-the-worlds-oldest-tortoise-his-dna-could-reveal-hints-to-longevity-180989663/</guid></item><item><title>这枚独一无二的青铜戒指让您可以一睹亚历山大灯塔的迷人风采，这是古代世界失落的奇迹</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-one-of-a-kind-bronze-ring-offers-a-tantalizing-glimpse-at-the-lighthouse-of-alexandria-a-lost-wonder-of-the-ancient-world-180989661/</link><description>埃及考古学家在安蒂罗多斯岛进行挖掘时发现了图章戒指，该岛曾经拥有一座奢华的托勒密宫殿</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:21:52 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-one-of-a-kind-bronze-ring-offers-a-tantalizing-glimpse-at-the-lighthouse-of-alexandria-a-lost-wonder-of-the-ancient-world-180989661/</guid></item><item><title>一个世纪前，在建造狮身人面像的岩石中发现了一个已灭绝的鳄鱼头骨。事实证明，它属于一个新物种</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-century-ago-an-extinct-crocidilians-skull-was-found-in-the-rocks-that-built-the-sphinx-turns-out-it-belonged-to-a-new-species-180989641/</link><description>根据一项新的研究，该标本长期以来被贴错标签。古生物学家将其鉴定为一种先前未被描述的鳄类属和种，是鳄鱼和短吻鳄的近亲，他们以古埃及神荷鲁斯的名字命名。</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-century-ago-an-extinct-crocidilians-skull-was-found-in-the-rocks-that-built-the-sphinx-turns-out-it-belonged-to-a-new-species-180989641/</guid></item><item><title>9月份的臭氧空洞是25年来最大的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/septembers-ozone-hole-was-the-biggest-it-has-been-in-25-years-180989657/</link><description>平流层臭氧层空洞的大小每年都会波动，但上个月的空洞特别大，面积为 1060 万平方英里</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:55:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/septembers-ozone-hole-was-the-biggest-it-has-been-in-25-years-180989657/</guid></item><item><title>由社区主导的苏格兰小岛上的考古发掘出土了一座具有“国际重要性”的中世纪修道院</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-community-led-archaeology-dig-on-a-tiny-scottish-isle-has-unearthed-a-medieval-monastery-of-international-importance-180989654/</link><description>该定居点由一位早期基督教圣人在 500 年代建立，“远远不仅仅是一座小岛上的教堂”。它在英国基督教化过程中发挥的作用可能比历史学家曾经意识到的更大</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:35:25 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-community-led-archaeology-dig-on-a-tiny-scottish-isle-has-unearthed-a-medieval-monastery-of-international-importance-180989654/</guid></item><item><title>这些南美鸟类的声音可与手提钻震耳欲聋的声音相媲美，使它们成为世界上已知最响亮的鸟类之一</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-south-american-birds-can-match-a-jackhammers-ear-splitting-volume-making-them-some-of-the-worlds-loudest-known-avians-180989629/</link><description>裸喉钟鸟和红腿鸫可以发出超过 120 分贝的声音，这使它们与吹喇叭的大象或电锯相当</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-south-american-birds-can-match-a-jackhammers-ear-splitting-volume-making-them-some-of-the-worlds-loudest-known-avians-180989629/</guid></item><item><title>德国考古学家在森林地面以下几英寸处出土了一座可能供奉战神火星的罗马神庙</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/just-inches-below-the-forest-floor-archaeologists-in-germany-unearthed-a-roman-temple-likely-dedicated-to-mars-the-god-of-war-180989650/</link><description>研究人员在卡珀斯堡堡垒附近挖掘时发现了该建筑的遗迹以及雕像碎片，卡珀斯堡堡垒是位于现代法兰克福郊区的古罗马军事防御工事</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 19:32:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/just-inches-below-the-forest-floor-archaeologists-in-germany-unearthed-a-roman-temple-likely-dedicated-to-mars-the-god-of-war-180989650/</guid></item><item><title>JMW 特纳 (JMW Turner) 在近 200 年前绘制了这幅令人惊叹的罗马风景画。如果你仔细看，你还能看到他的指纹</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/jmw-turner-painted-this-breathtaking-roman-landscape-nearly-200-years-ago-if-you-look-closely-you-can-still-see-his-fingerprints-180989659/</link><description>这位浪漫主义画家于1830年代完成了《罗马，来自阿文丁山》。这件作品成为他 2014 年最昂贵的艺术品，预计 12 月的售价将再创纪录</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 18:56:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/jmw-turner-painted-this-breathtaking-roman-landscape-nearly-200-years-ago-if-you-look-closely-you-can-still-see-his-fingerprints-180989659/</guid></item></channel></rss>